        "gcpCoordinateBasis": "Direct same-sheet settlement/lake anchors on Tornau's 1240–1533 main map. The 1462 controls are retained and expanded north/east using Lake Onega, Vyatka, Cherdyn, Kazan and interior northern controls visible on the same source sheet. No modern political border or cross-sheet registration is used; 220 km uncertainty intentionally dominates manual source-edge reading and atlas generalization. The northwest source area is explicitly triangulated between Pskov, Novgorod, Lake Onega and the same-sheet northern interior controls; the traced boundary itself is unchanged. Lake Peipus is added as a direct same-sheet natural-feature control west of Pskov; this encloses the source-traced northwest edge without moving the traced boundary. Lake Peipus is also triangulated directly to Lake Onega and the northern interior control, covering the source-traced northwest arc around [585,565] without altering the source ring. Lake Ladoga is added as a direct same-sheet natural-feature control; together with Lake Peipus, Lake Onega and the northern interior control it encloses the traced source arc around [620,520] without moving the ring. The clearly recognizable eastern shore of Lake Onega is added as a same-sheet natural-feature control at the traced northern edge; this pins the source vertex directly rather than extrapolating it. Triangles are normalized to a complete Delaunay mesh of the explicit same-sheet GCP set. Nine coarse outer-ring vertices that lay outside the GCP convex hull are conservatively moved inward to the nearest registered hull edge (by at most ~43 source pixels), rather than extrapolated. This inward clipping is fully dominated by the declared 220 km uncertainty.",
